Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:04.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Social navigation robots have to move safely through crowds,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.60,0:00:09.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and that means perceiving and predicting the paths of the people around them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.86,0:00:12.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper introduces the SiT dataset,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.46,0:00:16.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}short for Socially Interactive Pedestrian Trajectory.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.08,0:00:23.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Unlike earlier trajectory datasets captured from fixed rooftop cameras or from cars driving on separate roads,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.59,0:00:30.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}SiT was recorded by a mobile robot navigating densely populated indoor and outdoor spaces in downtown Seoul,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.97,0:00:34.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}capturing genuine human-robot interaction up close.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.46,0:00:39.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It ships synchronized LiDAR, camera, IMU, and RTK data with 2D and 3D annotations,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.06,0:00:44.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}semantic maps, and a full benchmark spanning 3D detection, tracking,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.71,0:00:48.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}trajectory prediction, and end-to-end motion forecasting.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.90,0:00:51.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For a robot to navigate safely among people,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.78,0:00:57.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it needs to perceive nearby pedestrians as individual entities in three-dimensional space
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.61,0:01:00.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and predict where they will move next.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.10,0:01:06.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The problem is that the datasets used to train these models don't reflect the robot's real situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.72,0:01:09.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Popular pedestrian datasets like ETH, UCY,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.47,0:01:14.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and SDD were captured by fixed cameras mounted high on rooftops or drones,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.32,0:01:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so they never see human-robot interaction.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.07,0:01:21.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Large autonomous-driving datasets do provide rich sensor data,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.14,0:01:28.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but there the vehicle and the pedestrians usually travel on separate roads and rarely come into close contact.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.34,0:01:33.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Neither setting matches a robot weaving through a crowded hallway or crosswalk.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.82,0:01:39.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Studies of human-robot interaction show that a robot's motion changes how nearby people walk,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.82,0:01:46.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and these effects are strongest when the robot and pedestrians share the same space at close distance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.39,0:01:47.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To study and model that,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.94,0:01:52.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}we need data collected while a robot actually moves through crowds,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.26,0:01:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}not from a camera bolted to a building.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.77,0:02:01.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Earlier robot datasets came close but each had a gap: STCrowd kept its sensors at a fixed position,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.16,0:02:02.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so scenes barely varied,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.70,0:02:09.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and JRDB did not organize its data into trajectories and did not fully synchronize its multiple sensors in time,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.92,0:02:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which limits sensor fusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.67,0:02:14.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}SiT is designed specifically to fill these gaps.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.06,0:02:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The SiT dataset makes several contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.98,0:02:23.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It provides large-scale real-world pedestrian trajectories gathered as a robot navigated
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.83,0:02:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}densely populated indoor and outdoor environments,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.15,0:02:31.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}from building interiors and campuses to crosswalks and public walkways.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.87,0:02:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It lets researchers build prediction models using rich context,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.06,0:02:41.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}including appearance features, the robot's ego-motion, and semantic map data.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.17,0:02:48.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It achieves precise time synchronization between all sensor modalities using a centralized triggering method,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.42,0:02:50.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which makes sensor fusion practical.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.81,0:02:55.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It supplies multi-layered semantic maps for both indoor and outdoor scenes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.79,0:03:01.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And it offers a curated benchmark covering 3D detection, 3D multi-object tracking,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.24,0:03:06.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}trajectory prediction, and an end-to-end task from perception to motion forecasting,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.82,0:03:09.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with everything released publicly.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.38,0:03:13.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The data was captured with a Clearpath Husky unmanned ground vehicle,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.03,0:03:16.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}remotely operated through downtown Seoul.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.79,0:03:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The robot carried two sixteen-channel Velodyne LiDARs,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.42,0:03:24.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}five Basler cameras arranged to cover a full 360 degrees,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.26,0:03:28.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}two inertial measurement units, and real-time kinematic positioning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.84,0:03:31.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To fuse camera and LiDAR reliably,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.13,0:03:38.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a pulse-per-second signal generator triggers all the sensors so their data is accurately aligned in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.20,0:03:44.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The robot's own pose is recovered from RTK outdoors and from a LiDAR-inertial SLAM algorithm indoors,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.00,0:03:51.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which is needed to compensate for the robot's ego-motion when forming pedestrian trajectories
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.26,0:03:53.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and to align the semantic maps.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.35,0:03:59.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Those maps use a twelve-layer hierarchical structure built from point clouds and segmented by hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.01,0:04:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Expert annotators labeled 3D cuboids at five hertz,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.45,0:04:06.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which were interpolated up to ten hertz,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.14,0:04:10.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and 2D boxes were generated from the 3D cuboids that share object IDs.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.85,0:04:14.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For privacy, all faces and license plates are blurred.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.79,0:04:16.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In total, SiT contains 60 scenes,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.92,0:04:22.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which amounts to about sixty thousand images and twelve thousand point cloud frames,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.34,0:04:27.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}carrying roughly four hundred and seventy thousand two-dimensional annotations and three
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.02,0:04:31.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}hundred and twenty thousand three-dimensional annotations.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.76,0:04:36.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Each clip is twenty seconds of sequential data sampled at ten hertz,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.15,0:04:40.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}producing nine seconds of trajectory represented as pose vectors.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.34,0:04:43.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On top of this data, the paper defines four benchmarks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.89,0:04:51.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Three-D pedestrian detection is scored with average precision based on center distance at thresholds of a quarter,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.25,0:04:52.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a half, one, and two meters.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.06,0:04:56.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Three-D tracking uses standard multi-object tracking metrics.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.99,0:05:02.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Trajectory prediction takes two seconds of past motion and predicts seven seconds ahead,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.67,0:05:08.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}scored with average and final displacement error over the best of K candidate trajectories.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.54,0:05:14.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And an end-to-end task runs from raw sensors all the way to future bounding boxes and trajectories.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.23,0:05:20.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The data analysis confirms that SiT captures exactly the interactions it set out to.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.72,0:05:26.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}When you plot where pedestrians appear relative to the robot, they cluster close in,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.20,0:05:27.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}from all directions,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.51,0:05:33.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}whereas in Waymo Open and nuScenes pedestrians tend to sit off to the side on separate paths.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.59,0:05:40.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Counting instances that satisfy both a space-sharing condition and a within-two-meter proximity condition,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.51,0:05:44.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}SiT has dramatically more than the three autonomous-driving datasets,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.02,0:05:52.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which means driving data underrepresents the human-robot interaction that social navigation robots must handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.27,0:05:53.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the benchmark itself,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.84,0:06:00.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the standout finding is that supplying the semantic map improves trajectory prediction: the best model,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.56,0:06:01.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}NSP-SFM with the map,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.94,0:06:06.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reaches an ADE-twenty of about 0.52 and an FDE-twenty of about 0.93,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.38,0:06:09.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}clearly better than the same model without the map.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.01,0:06:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The most informative comparison in the paper is turning the semantic map on and off for trajectory prediction.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.62,0:06:19.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For Y-Net,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.22,0:06:23.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}adding the map lowers the ADE-twenty from about 0.84 down to 0.68 and the FDE-twenty from about 1.88 to 1.55.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.83,0:06:28.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For NSP-SFM,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.43,0:06:32.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the map brings ADE-twenty from about 0.63 to 0.52 and FDE-twenty from about 1.09 to 0.93.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.04,0:06:37.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In both cases the map helps,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.64,0:06:42.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}confirming the value of the scene context that SiT provides.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.25,0:06:46.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the detection side,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.85,0:06:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}models that fuse camera and LiDAR outperform single-sensor models,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.46,0:06:55.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and voxel-based backbones outperform pillar-based ones,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.06,0:07:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with TransFusion using a voxel backbone giving the best detection score.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.97,0:07:04.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Here are the numbers worth remembering.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.04,0:07:09.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}SiT has sixty scenes,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.11,0:07:13.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}about sixty thousand images and twelve thousand point cloud frames,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.18,0:07:17.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with roughly four hundred and seventy thousand two-dimensional and three hundred and twenty
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.25,0:07:21.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}thousand three-dimensional annotations.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.32,0:07:25.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the trajectory benchmark,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.39,0:07:29.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the best model with the semantic map reaches an ADE-twenty of about 0.52 and an FDE-twenty of about 0.93.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.46,0:07:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On detection,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.53,0:07:37.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the best camera-plus-LiDAR fusion model reaches a mean average precision of about 0.53.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.60,0:07:41.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And on tracking, the CenterPoint tracker leads with an sAMOTA around 0.61.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.97,0:07:43.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The takeaway is simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.36,0:07:47.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}If you want to build robots that move safely and gracefully among people,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.78,0:07:51.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}you need training data that shows the robot up close in the crowd,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.77,0:07:56.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with all its sensors aligned in time and with the surrounding scene captured as a map.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.98,0:08:00.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}SiT is the first dataset to deliver that combination,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.19,0:08:04.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}together with a benchmark that spans detection, tracking, prediction,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.36,0:08:05.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and end-to-end forecasting,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.00,0:08:09.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it is all publicly released so the community can build on it.
